how's it going everybody it's warren  welcome back to my channel the cosmic  wonder where we talk all things marvel  and lately we've been learning  a lot of new information about the  marvel  cinematic universe specifically things  that we could have never known about  before because they weren't released  on screen these are things happening in  the mcu but off screen that we never had  a chance to learn about until  now if you caught my video yesterday  about shuri possibly becoming the new  black panther and creating a new  heart-shaped herb then you heard me talk  about a new  marvel cinematic universe tie-in book  called the wakanda files  now basically what it means by a tie-in  book means that anything that has  happened in the book  has happened in the mcu we just didn't  see it but what it's doing is telling  us what's going on in the background in  places like wakanda while the events of  the avengers happened  and there are some pretty cool reveals  in this book and one of those things  that has been revealed  is how tony stark discovered spider-man  was  insanely impressed by him and the plans  that he had for him  this was never revealed until now and  i'll go over the whole entire thing but  real quick if you're new be sure to  subscribe so you don't miss out on any  of the latest mcu news and so you can  enter this week's giveaway for a chance  to win an  imposter spider-man funko pop so when  spider-man was first introduced into the  marvel cinematic universe he was  introduced in captain america civil war  and we kind of got a backstory for him  but we didn't get his origin we didn't  see the radioactive spider  we essentially just saw some youtube  videos of spider-man protecting and  saving people  and according to the wakanda files  that's what tony saw at first too  and he decided to do some of his own  investigating  in the book tony stark writes this down  himself about peter parker he says  this kid in queens that's blowing up on  youtube is a bit more interesting than a  cat playing a harmonica  get this some teenager gets bit by a  spider and suddenly shows up some of the  best in the avengers squad  and i don't think these are special  effects this kid is catching an  in-motion vehicle traveling at 45 miles  per hour  that's like 3 000 pounds worth of  vehicle  how so right away tony is already super  impressed and really  amazed but one thing that's really  interesting here is that he mentions a  spider  something that we've never heard with  tom holland spider-man so although they  didn't show us the spider bite like they  have in pretty much almost every other  spider-man  that is still indeed how spider-man got  his powers they did not change that part  but tony stark goes on to do entry logs  about spider-man and he realizes that  he's created his own  webbing and he says he's created this  webbing from what  over-the-counter products he's buying in  a bodega if he created  all of this tech scrapping together  garbage think what he could do with the  playground we've built upstate  so this is where tony saw the entire  vision he saw spider-man joining the  avengers he saw spider-man going to  upstate new york to the avengers  facility and working on a new spider  suit because we all saw  the first spider suit that he had in  spider-man homecoming lordy  can you even see in these yes yes  but as it turns out tony stark actually  created the nanotech  iron spider suit as sort of a bargaining  method to get peter parker to join the  avengers  it was kind of like an incentive it was  kind of like hey if you join us you get  this really awesome suit  in his next log he says once he's got  the hang of the upgrades let's lend him  a hand  or four if we give him nanotech spider  legs that build out from his back  it can be a safeguard from falling a  defense mechanism we won't get carried  away like cross did with that  yellowjacket suit but  it could be a fun touch so two very  interesting things here  one is that the iron spider legs that  come out of the iron spider suit were  kind of a fail-safe for tony  now by this point in time he was kind of  protecting peter parker he was already  his mentor and he wanted to make sure  more than  anything that he didn't get hurt so the  legs were protection for peter parker if  he fell from a very far height which we  actually saw happen in avengers in game  and then we saw the instant kill mode  but another interesting thing is that it  seems like the iron spider suit was  influenced just  a little bit by the yellow jacket suit  not anything of significant importance  but interesting nonetheless  and in his last vlog when he's talking  to friday he says  let's mock up a prototype and dangle it  in front of the kid  just as a little incentive to keep on  the straight and narrow  should he ever want to join the avengers  so these are tony stark's direct  thoughts on peter parker  coming straight from his log and as you  can see he was extremely impressed with  him  right away from the beginning and it's  funny to see how much tony actually  wanted peter parker to join the avengers  for a pretty long time  when he was ready of course although  tony of course wanted him to become an  avenger at the end of spider-man  homecoming  but peter declined despite the really  awesome suit but as we can see from very  early on tony stark thought a lot about  peter parker and it definitely seemed  like to tony stark  peter parker was his protege someone who  he could train and mentor and possibly  go on to take on his mantle in the  future  but most importantly peter parker was  somebody that tony stark  deeply cared about which is why he made  things like the iron spider legs to  protect him  but let me know what you think about  this and be sure to subscribe because  i'll be going over  more details from the wakanda files mcu  time book  soon don't forget to like the video and  for live updates you can always follow  me on instagram